            <div xml:id="d551">

                <pb facs="0449" n="437" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg437"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.515/73: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Hibbard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-08-29T16:00:00-04:00">August 29, 1942—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>211. Your 269, August 21, 10 a.m. Department’s 187, August 3, 8 p.m., and 188,
                    August 3, 9 p.m. The agreement for acquisition of British current coin in
                    exchange for U. S. current coin is contained in Department’s 187. The statements
                    contained in Department’s 188 simply explained why certain provisions were
                    contained in the proposed agreement. The explanations do not and should not form
                    a part of the agreement. Accordingly the Treasury does not wish to confirm the
                    agreement as stated in your No. 269. You are requested to ask the Liberian
                    Government to confirm the agreement as stated in Department’s 187.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
